            ("What type of concrete involves threading steel cables through internal plastic ducts after the concrete has cured, tensioning them with hydraulic jacks?", "Post-tensioned Concrete", ["Pre-tensioned Concrete", "Conventional Rebar Concrete", "Cast-in-Place Concrete"], "Post-tensioning allows long, slender bridge spans and thin parking garage slabs to carry immense loads without sag."),
