            ("What mechanical property defines a material\'s ability to undergo significant plastic deformation under tensile stress before fracturing (e.g., drawing into wires)?", "Ductility", ["Brittleness", "Hardness", "Malleability"], "Ductility is measured by percent elongation or percent reduction in area; ductile metals (copper, mild steel) display substantial necking."),
