            ("What heat treatment introduces carbon or nitrogen into the outer surface of a low-carbon steel part to produce a hard, wear-resistant outer shell with a tough core?", "Case Hardening (Carburizing / Nitriding)", ["Through Hardening", "Full Annealing", "Spheroidizing"], "Carburizing gears produces a glass-hard outer case (HRC 60) to resist tooth contact wear while retaining a ductile core to absorb shock."),
