            ("What layered lamellar microstructure in carbon steel forms upon slow cooling through the eutectoid point, composed of alternating plates of ferrite and cementite?", "Pearlite", ["Martensite", "Bainite", "Austenite"], "Pearlite forms at 727 C under slow furnace cooling, resembling mother-of-pearl under optical magnification."),
            ("What electrochemical corrosion mechanism occurs when two dissimilar metals are in direct electrical contact within the presence of a conductive electrolyte?", "Galvanic Corrosion", ["Pitting Corrosion", "Crevice Corrosion", "Intergranular Corrosion"], "The more active (anodic) metal corrodes rapidly to protect the more noble (cathodic) metal (e.g., zinc corroding to protect steel)."),
            ("What corrosion protection technique connects an easily corroded sacrificial metal (such as zinc or magnesium) to protect a submerged steel hull or pipeline?", "Cathodic Protection (Sacrificial Anode)", ["Anodic Passivation", "Galvanic Coupling", "Electroless Plating"], "Sacrificial zinc anodes sacrifice themselves by donating electrons to the steel hull, maintaining steel in an uncorroded cathodic state."),
            ("What chemical element is alloyed into carbon steel at a concentration of at least 10.5% to create self-healing, corrosion-resistant Stainless Steel?", "Chromium (Cr)", ["Nickel (Ni)", "Molybdenum (Mo)", "Titanium (Ti)"], "Chromium reacts with atmospheric oxygen to form an invisible, tenacious, self-healing passive surface layer of chromium oxide (Cr2O3)."),
            ("What slow, time-dependent, permanent plastic deformation occurs in structural materials subjected to continuous mechanical stress at elevated temperatures?", "Creep", ["Fatigue", "Stress Relaxation", "Thermal Shock"], "Creep becomes critical in jet engine turbine blades and steam boilers operating at temperatures exceeding 40% of absolute melting point (Tm)."),
            ("What advanced composite material consists of high-strength carbon fibers embedded within an epoxy polymer resin matrix, offering exceptional strength-to-weight ratios?", "Carbon Fiber Reinforced Polymer (CFRP)", ["Fiberglass (GFRP)", "Kevlar Aramid", "Metal Matrix Composite"], "CFRP composites are utilized extensively in modern commercial airliners (Boeing 787, Airbus A350) to cut structural airframe weight."),
