            ("What thermal state transition marks where an amorphous solid polymer changes from a hard, brittle, glassy state to a soft, rubbery, flexible state?", "Glass Transition Temperature (Tg)", ["Melting Temperature (Tm)", "Crystallization Temperature", "Heat Deflection Temperature"], "Below Tg, polymer chain molecular mobility is frozen (rigid); above Tg, secondary bonds loosen, allowing chain segment flexibility."),
            ("What class of cross-linked polymers permanently set into rigid shapes upon heating and cannot be remelted without chemical decomposition?", "Thermosetting Polymers (Thermosets, e.g., Epoxy, Phenolic)", ["Thermoplastics (e.g., Polyethylene)", "Elastomers", "Liquid Crystal Polymers"], "Thermosets form irreversible covalent chemical cross-links during curing, resisting heat and solvents without melting."),
            ("What class of linear or branched polymers can be repeatedly melted, reshaped, and solidified upon heating and cooling without chemical degradation?", "Thermoplastics (e.g., Polypropylene, Nylon)", ["Thermosetting Polymers", "Vulcanized Rubbers", "Phenolic Resins"], "Thermoplastics feature intermolecular secondary bonds that soften under heat, enabling rapid injection molding and recycling."),
            ("What chemical cross-linking process heats natural rubber with sulfur to form cross-links between polymer chains, improving elasticity and thermal stability?", "Vulcanization", ["Polymerization", "Sintering", "Extrusion"], "Discovered by Charles Goodyear in 1839, sulfur bridges prevent rubber chains from sliding, transforming sticky latex into resilient tire rubber."),
            ("What high-temperature manufacturing process compacts and bonds powdered metal or ceramic particles below their melting point through solid-state atomic diffusion?", "Sintering", ["Forging", "Investment Casting", "Extrusion"], "Sintering fuses powder metallurgy parts and high-tech ceramics into dense, strong components without melting the entire mass.")
