            ("What is 'Touch Potential' (Touch Voltage) in electrical safety analysis around high-voltage substations?", "The potential difference between a person's hand touching an energized metal structure and their feet touching the ground", ["The voltage felt between both feet during a fault", "The static shock felt when touching a doorknob", "The voltage drop across an electrical resistor"], "Substation grounding grids are designed with crushed stone and buried copper mesh to keep touch potential below lethal physiological levels."),
