            ("What electrical hazard occurs when high-frequency electromagnetic fields from power cables induce hazardous voltages on adjacent ungrounded metal pipelines?", "Induced Voltage Hazard", ["Static Electricity Discharge", "Direct Short Circuit", "Thermal Breakdown"], "Parallel utility corridors induce continuous AC voltages on unbonded gas pipelines, presenting severe shock risks to pipeline workers."),
            ("What is the primary safety purpose of installing an equipment grounding conductor in an extension cord or portable tool cord (three-prong plug)?", "To ground the exposed metal housing of the tool so that an internal wire short trips the breaker rather than shocking the operator", ["To provide return current for motor speed control", "To reduce electromagnetic noise on the power line", "To increase tool motor torque output"], "If an internal energized conductor touches the metal frame of a grounded drill, current rushes to ground, tripping the breaker in milliseconds."),
            ("What designation indicates an electrical power tool that has two complete layers of electrical insulation between live parts and exterior surfaces, eliminating the need for a ground prong?", "Double Insulated (marked with a square inside a square symbol)", ["Explosion Proof", "GFCI Protected", "Intrinsically Safe"], "Double-insulated tools utilize non-conductive plastic outer enclosures and reinforced motor insulation, safe to use with two-prong cords."),
            ("What term describes electrical apparatus designed so that under normal or abnormal conditions, any electrical spark or thermal effect is incapable of causing ignition of explosive atmospheres?", "Intrinsically Safe (IS)", ["Explosion Proof", "Dust Ignitionproof", "Non-Incendive"], "Intrinsically safe circuits limit electrical and thermal energy below the minimum ignition threshold of flammable gases (petroleum refineries, mines)."),
            ("What type of heavy cast-metal electrical enclosure is engineered to contain an internal explosion of gas without allowing flames to ignite the surrounding explosive atmosphere?", "Explosion-Proof Enclosure (NEMA 7 / 9)", ["Intrinsically Safe Enclosure", "Weatherproof NEMA 4X Enclosure", "Dust-Tight Enclosure"], "Explosion-proof enclosures feature heavy threaded joints and ground flat flanged flame paths that cool escaping gases before they reach ambient air."),
            ("What is the maximum body resistance typically assumed for an adult human in dry conditions when calculating electrical shock current?", "Approximately 1,000 to 100,000 Ohms (dropping to 500-1,000 Ohms when wet or skin is punctured)", ["10 Ohms", "1,000,000 Ohms", "Zero Ohms"], "Dry intact skin provides substantial resistance; moisture, sweat, or high voltage breaks down skin barrier resistance to ~1,000 Ohms."),
            ("Why is DC current generally more dangerous than AC current regarding muscle release, but AC current more prone to triggering ventricular fibrillation?", "DC current causes sustained tetanic muscle contraction with continuous gripping; 60 Hz AC current aligns with the vulnerable T-wave phase of heart repolarization", ["DC current causes high-frequency nerve burns", "AC current repels human skin naturally", "DC current vibrates human bones"], "60 Hz AC disrupts myocardial electrochemical pacing at low current levels (50-100 mA), whereas DC locks muscles in continuous contraction."),
            ("What safety device in an electrical substation connects high-voltage equipment directly to the ground grid during de-energized maintenance to protect against accidental re-energization?", "Portable Safety Grounding Clamps (Grounding Cluster)", ["High-voltage surge arrester", "Station battery disconnect", "Capacitor trip unit"], "Grounding clusters create a solid low-impedance short circuit to earth, guaranteeing that accidental re-energization trips upstream breakers instantly."),
            ("What personal safety habit should an electrical worker adopt regarding personal jewelry (rings, watches, necklaces) before servicing electrical panels?", "Remove all metal rings, wristwatches, metal-framed glasses, and necklaces before opening panels", ["Tape over rings with transparent tape", "Wear rubber gloves over metal watches", "Leave jewelry on if made of silver"], "Metal rings and watch bands bridging an energized terminal to ground melt instantly into human flesh, causing third-degree burns and amputation."),
