            ("What dangerous thermal event occurs in lead-acid or lithium-ion battery banks when charging heat generation exceeds heat dissipation capacity?", "Thermal Runaway", ["Sulfation", "Electrolytic Stratification", "Plate Buckling"], "Internal heat increases chemical reaction rates, drawing higher charging current that escalates temperatures until battery fire or explosion occurs."),
            ("What toxic and explosive gas is vented by lead-acid storage battery banks during high-rate float charging and overcharging, requiring dedicated room ventilation?", "Hydrogen gas (H2)", ["Carbon Monoxide", "Chlorine gas", "Sulfur Hexafluoride"], "Electrolysis of water dissociates battery electrolyte into explosive hydrogen and oxygen; hydrogen concentrations above 4% risk room explosion.")
